apx for Debian
==============

Differences from an upstream "make install":

* The configuration is installed as /etc/apx/config.json. Upstream's Makefile
  writes /etc/apx/apx.json, but apx only reads config.json, so a subsystem
  built that way finds no stacks.

* distrobox is bundled, in /usr/share/apx/distrobox/, and is the copy apx
  drives. Debian's own distrobox package is separate and unaffected.

* apx ships no stacks. Install apx-stacks for a default set, or drop your own
  YAML files into /usr/share/apx/stacks or ~/.local/share/apx/stacks.

apx uses podman if it is installed and Docker otherwise. Rootless podman needs
uidmap, which is why this package depends on it.

 -- Matthew Lenz <matthewlenz@gmail.com>  Sun, 20 Sep 2026 19:07:12 -0500
